# Git Safety — Never Destroy the Working Directory

**NEVER run `git clean`, `git checkout --orphan`, or any command that removes untracked files from the main working directory.**

Gitignored files (`.local-config.json`, `.venv/`, `data/`, `Experiments/`) are untracked and will be permanently destroyed by those commands.

## Banned commands (in the main worktree)

- `git clean` (any flags)
- `git checkout --orphan`
- `git reset --hard` to a commit that predates untracked work
- `rm -rf` targeting the workspace root or broad directories

## Safe alternatives

- Orphan branches: `git worktree add /tmp/<name> --orphan <branch>`
- Temporary checkouts: `git worktree add /tmp/<name> <branch>`
- Cleaning caches: delete a specific directory (`rm -rf .pytest_cache/`), never `git clean`

## Context

A `git checkout --orphan` + `git clean -fd` sequence on `unity-pga-ai-assisted-balancing` on 2026-03-29 wiped gitignored files. Assume `data/` and `Experiments/` are destructible.
